"""Asset tables are held by gangs.

``AssetTable`` is a table of one Holding asset type's assets — the core
rulebook's Territory Selection Table — with ``dice`` for the die it is
rolled on, and ``AssetTableEntry`` one asset on it with the band of rolls
that lands there. A table is assignable because holding one is what says
a gang may roll on it, so ``DefaultAssignment``, ``AddsAssignable`` and
``RemovesAssignable`` each gain one nullable ``asset_table`` key, and the
exactly-one constraints are restated to admit it.

Reversible: the tables and the keys go.
"""

